title: v5.37.12 — fail-closed portal compliance security patch
summary: 'Five fail-open auth-bypass scenarios closed in Paradigm''s portal compliance pipeline. Field report from downstream project (Quakeee-web, 2026-04-21) identified 3 bugs; security audit surfaced a 5th scenario (bash `|| true` masking all compliance failures) rated CRITICAL. Team orchestration: reviewer (per-bug root cause), Explore (blast radius), Jinx (systemic reflection — admitted v5.37.11 prevention plan was insufficient), security (auth-bypass audit + non-negotiable bundle order), architect (comprehensive plan), builder (implementation), reviewer validation pass. Scope: fail-closed semantics + Object.keys(Gate[]) fix + safeLoad<T>() wrapper with error-message redaction + discriminated-union loadPortalConfig + first tests/ in paradigm CLI package. Two regression suites (25 new tests). Deliberately excluded from this release (defers to v5.38.0): Bug 1 prefix parser, writeAndConfirm wrapper, round-trip consistency manifest, PARADIGM_STRICT flag, site-doc fixes, near-match suggestion engine.'
